\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 9. Multiple schemas with 
\f4\fs39 Union
\f0\fs36 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 CineBot books tickets. What happens when someone asks it to cancel? And what about modify, update, shift, check \'97 ten different intents?\
Rather than one schema with an intent field, or ten separate agents, hand the model several schemas and let it pick:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 union_agent = create_agent(\
    model="openai:gpt-5-mini",\
    tools=[],\
    response_format=ToolStrategy(schema=Union[NewBooking, CancelBooking]),\
)\
\
result = union_agent.invoke(\{"messages": [\{"role": "user", "content": "I want to cancel my Oppenheimer booking"\}]\})\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Asked to cancel, it returned a 
\f3\fs26 CancelBooking
\f1\fs24 . Asked to book, 
\f3\fs26 NewBooking
\f1\fs24 . The field descriptions on each class are what the model reads to choose.\
Consuming the result:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 if isinstance(result["structured_response"], NewBooking):\
    ...\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Union only works under 
\f4\fs26 ToolStrategy
\f0\fs24 .
\f1\b0  Checking the docs live during class showed 
\f3\fs26 ProviderStrategy.schema
\f1\fs24  does not accept a union; the tool-calling path does. Each new intent still needs its own Pydantic class \'97 none of this is automatic.\
Guidance from Q&A: five to seven schemas is reasonable. Beyond that, move to a multi-agent architecture instead of stuffing everything into one union.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

