\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 11. Q&A worth keeping\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Business logic vs framework logic.
\f1\b0  If a user asks for 15 tickets and the cap is 10, whether to silently book 10 or return an error is a product decision, not a LangChain one. Use 
\f3\fs26 handle_errors=False
\f1\fs24  plus 
\f3\fs26 try
\f1\fs24 /
\f3\fs26 except
\f1\fs24  when you want to surface the error to the user. Compare Amazon's cart, which shows "only 12 available" instead of crashing.\

\f0\b Authenticated tools (banking example).
\f1\b0  Treat tools as ordinary API calls and keep auth inside the function. For anything needing the end user to authenticate at runtime, the pattern is 
\f0\b headless tools
\f1\b0  \'97 tools that execute on the user's side, the way ChatGPT bounces you to Google for OAuth. Alternatively make the tools incremental: call an auth tool first, then the balance tool. Human-in-the-loop covers the "which of your five accounts?" case.\

\f0\b Memory persistence.
\f1\b0  Checkpointers can be in-memory or backed by a database. Which one depends on the use case: short-term memory can live in RAM, long-term should persist. Don't blindly reload every stored message into state \'97 Claude's strength is fetching only the messages it needs. Full coverage of memory, checkpointing, and 
\f3\fs26 RunnableConfig
\f1\fs24  comes later, with a project after RAG and another after memory.\

\f0\b Model-to-strategy mapping.
\f1\b0  For an app supporting several models, a plain dictionary mapping model name 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  strategy is fine. Adding a new model is a code change; that's normal.\

\f0\b Multiple different errors on one schema.
\f1\b0  Not supported through repeated 
\f3\fs26 handle_errors
\f1\fs24  arguments. Use the callable form and branch inside your own function, or validate again outside the framework. He mentioned running his own custom error class on top of the framework's output back in the 
\f3\fs26 text-davinci-003
\f1\fs24  days.\

\f0\b Framework choice for enterprise.
\f1\b0  No framework is inherently good or bad. When someone said their architect found LangChain bloated for a latency-sensitive edge application, the suggestion was to evaluate 
\f0\b Google ADK
\f1\b0  as a leaner alternative with comparable features.\

\f0\b Chasing job titles.
\f1\b0  On FDE, "harness engineering", "graph engineering" and similar: these are mostly new labels on the same concepts. Learn to build agents properly and you qualify for all of them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
